@title A wire that breaks the project's house wire rules is listed in Issues
@area Reports
# Accept one protective device's group under IEC 60204-1, then state house rules; those wires break them.
click_text "Open example"
wait 20
click_text Reports
wait 5
click_text "Bench output..."
wait 20
click_text Autopilot
wait 20
click_text "14 changes"
wait 5
click_text "Accept ticked in this group"
wait 10
click_text "Wire rules: IEC 60204-1"
wait 5
click_text "House rules"
wait 10
click_text "program default (1.5 mm²)"
wait 5
click_text "4 mm²"
wait 10
click_text "IEC 60204-1" #4
wait 5
click_text "VT"
wait 8
shot house-rules-set
key Escape
wait 5
click 935 50
wait 5
click_text "warnings"
wait 10
expect "the project's house rule gives VT"
expect "under the house minimum of 4 mm²"
shot issues-wire-rule
check_blank issues-wire-rule
check_layout
# A click on a row goes to the wire and marks it on the page.
click_text "Wire 3 (AC power circuit) is BK; the project's house rule gives VT"
wait 10
shot issue-wire-marked
check_blank issue-wire-marked
check_layout
